# Modifying existing production websites

This repo ships real static sites. Unless the user **explicitly approves** removal or replacement in the same conversation, agents must **not** delete, rename, or overwrite existing code, sections, UI, copy, styling, routes, APIs, environment variables, or deployment configuration.

- Preserve existing behavior unless the task requires changing it.
- Make the **smallest, most targeted** edits; no unrelated refactors, redesigns, or cleanup.
- No placeholder or fake functionality; if uncertain, **ask** before changing architecture or removing anything.
- **Before** editing: state which files or areas will change and why.
- **After** editing: summarize what changed factually.
- If the request cannot be met as stated, say so clearly instead of implying completion.

## Deployment

Follow **`warn-before-live-user-impact`**: **Deploy check** first, then deploy.

**Public** sites — deploy when the owner asked (**deploy** / **ship it** / **yes**).

**Owner-only** sites — verify per **`owner-only-auto-deploy`**, deploy in the same turn without waiting for those words.

When the user says **deploy** or **deploy now**, give the Deploy check, then run deploy immediately in the same turn. Do not add extra improvements before deploy unless required to fix a failure. If deploy fails, report the exact error and propose the smallest fix.

For kids static sites, deploy from repo root with `bash top/scripts/deploy-kids-sites.sh` (see `kids-sites-immediate-deploy` and `owner-only-auto-deploy`).
